.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
.TH RELIQUARY-TOOL 1 "" "reliquary @version@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reliquary\-tool \- manage Reliquary software security tokens
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reliquary\-tool
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B reliquary\-tool
.BR \-\-help | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reliquary\-tool
is the administrative command\-line client for Reliquary. It connects to
the per\-user Reliquary daemon over its control socket and manages
.IR tokens ,
each of which holds up to three key
.IR slots .
Once populated, tokens are exposed to applications as PKCS#11 objects and as
GnuPG OpenPGP cards (via
.BR reliquary\-scd\-proxy ).
.PP
Before a user can use
.BR reliquary\-tool ,
an administrator must provision that user's store directory once, as root,
with
.BR reliquary\-setup\-user (8).
Thereafter
.B reliquary\-tool
runs entirely as the unprivileged user, and
.B init
sets the store's admin PIN.
.PP
Commands that use private keys, and PIN changes, prompt for the relevant PIN
on the terminal with echo disabled. The daemon must already be running; if it
cannot be reached,
.B reliquary\-tool
prints an error and exits non\-zero.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize the store and set the admin PIN. Run once before any tokens are
created.
.TP
.BI "create " label
Create a new, empty token named
.IR label .
.TP
.BI "delete " label
Delete the token
.I label
and everything in it.
.TP
.BI "clear " label
Remove all key slots from
.IR label ,
leaving the token in place.
.TP
.BI "genkey " "label slot algorithm"
Generate a new key of
.I algorithm
in
.I slot
of
.IR label .
Prompts for the token PIN.
.TP
.BI "import-ssh " label " [" slot "] " keyfile
Import an unencrypted OpenSSH private key from
.IR keyfile .
When
.I slot
is given, import into that slot of the existing token
.IR label ,
prompting for its PIN. When
.I slot
is omitted, create a new token
.I label
holding the key in its
.B auth
slot, prompting for a new PIN.
.TP
.B list
List all tokens in the store.
.TP
.BI "info " label
Show details of
.IR label :
its serial number, slots, and key algorithms.
.TP
.BI "change-pin " label
Change the user PIN of
.IR label .
.TP
.BI "disconnect " label
Hide
.I label
from enumeration on the PKCS#11 and OpenPGP\-card faces, without deleting it.
.TP
.BI "connect " label
Make a previously disconnected token
.I label
visible again.
.TP
.BI "unblock " label
Reset the PIN retry counter of a locked token
.IR label .
Requires the admin PIN.
.SH "SLOTS AND ALGORITHMS"
Valid slot names are
.BR sign ", " encrypt ", and " auth .
.PP
Valid key algorithms are
.BR rsa2048 ", " rsa3072 ", " rsa4096 ", "
.BR nistp256 ", " nistp384 ", " nistp521 ", and " ed25519 .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RELIQUARY_SOCKET
If set, the daemon control socket path to use, overriding the default.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Locates the default control socket at
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/reliquary/socket .
Must be set unless
.B RELIQUARY_SOCKET
is given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/reliquary/socket
Default Reliquary daemon control socket.
.TP
.I @store_dir@/<uid>/
Per\-user token store managed through the daemon.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Returns 0 on success and non\-zero on error, including a wrong PIN, an unknown
command or token, or an unreachable daemon.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
These examples assume an administrator has already provisioned the user's
store as root with
.BR reliquary\-setup\-user (8),
and that it has been initialized once with
.BR "reliquary\-tool init" .
.PP
.B "As an OpenPGP card (GnuPG)."
With
.B gpg\-agent
configured to use
.B reliquary\-scd\-proxy
as its
.I scdaemon-program
(so the token appears as a card), create a token and move an existing subkey
onto it with
.BR keytocard :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
reliquary\-tool create gpg
gpg \-\-edit\-key alice@example.com
  # at the gpg> prompt: "key N" to select a subkey, then
  # "keytocard", choose the slot, and "save".
.EE
.RE
.PP
.B "As an SSH key via PKCS#11, imported."
Create a token, import an existing OpenSSH private key into its
.B auth
slot, and authenticate by pointing
.B ssh
at the module:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
reliquary\-tool create ssh
reliquary\-tool import\-ssh ssh auth ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
ssh \-I /usr/local/lib/pkcs11/reliquary-pkcs11.so user@host
.EE
.RE
.PP
.B "As an SSH key via PKCS#11, generated."
The same, but generate a fresh key on the token instead of importing one; its
public half must then be published to the server:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
reliquary\-tool create ssh
reliquary\-tool genkey ssh auth ed25519
ssh\-keygen \-D /usr/local/lib/pkcs11/reliquary-pkcs11.so   # add to authorized_keys
ssh \-I /usr/local/lib/pkcs11/reliquary-pkcs11.so user@host
.EE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR reliquary\-setup\-user (8),
.BR gpg (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1),
.BR ssh\-add (1),
.BR pkcs11\-tool (1)
